 DA:Cr1.1.4b, a look-for and a kept card: the challenge the student invented and the partner's solution shown, the element changed named on the card; DA:Cn10.1.4b, a look-for and kept notes: two or three key facts danced, each source named on the research notes, one reflection line; DA:Cn10.1.4a, a written item: an unseen described dance's main idea linked to an experience (the student's own or the invented child's), with how they are alike or different; DA:Cn11.1.4a, a written item: two moves of an unseen style on a new work card and how they reflect its place, era or community. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: several sources into one body of material and learning compared across subjects (grade 5). Tools: the idea card, challenge card, research notes sheet, source cards Curio Class writes from the science course's own sourced readings, work cards, Curio Class's own. Free path: pictures and music the class already has. Once-a-week path: 8 sessions | After unit 5 because an invented challenge is solved by changing the elements and rhythms just taught; before unit 7 because the study around one main idea starts from an idea card. The research-notes model starts here, and the topics come from science units taught by these weeks | Candidate: the source cards checked against the science course's readings, fact by fact | Gumboot dance: made by migrant mine workers who lived far from home under hard and unfair rules, said in one plain sentence from a South African cultural body's or a museum's page, read first by the sensitivity agent; no boots, no imitation of a people; students slap their own thighs gently and stamp softly in bare feet. Lerman: the work is studied only for how she worked with scientists; genes are not taught. Ties to the student's own life invited, never required, with the invented option; health's steps if a student tells something. Hazards and controls: as unit 1. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (moving). |
