ne moment of the dance; DA:Pr6.1.4a, a kept plan and a look-for: the stage plan, and the showing set up as planned; DA:Pr6.1.4b, a look-for and a kept line: the production element kept is used, and the program card says how it serves the dance's purpose. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: one dance fitted to two venues (grade 5), a change log (grade 5). Tools: the rework card, relationship sketch sheet, stage plan sheet and program card, Curio Class's own. Free path: a painted paper backdrop, chairs for the audience edge, a song or a drum. Once-a-week path: 5 sessions | Last in grade 4 because the dance reworked and staged is unit 7's study; the year-end check sits before it (week 26), outside the core checks of weeks 27 and 30 to 32, and this unit's family showing in weeks 27 to 32 is its own assessment | Candidate: a seated audience plan for a family member who uses a wheelchair, in every stage plan | Tallchief: of the Osage Nation, named as her own published words name her; the sensitivity agent reads the company's or a museum's page and an Osage Nation source first; no costume or imitation of the Firebird or of a people. Outdoors: the lawn checked for holes, sticks and glass; shade and water; the class stays in sight; bare feet only on checked grass. Light: no flashing, never pointed at eyes. Family yes for showing outside class; no photographs without it. Hazards and controls: as unit 1. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (moving). |
