ronize, project, body percussion, tight, flowing. Showing: the ensemble's body-percussion dance for a partner class. End-of-unit evidence (a showing day and a written day), id by id: DA:Pr5.1.5a, a look-for: a run of three phrases recalled with alignment and clarity; DA:Pr5.1.5c, a look-for and a kept card: unison timing and even spacing, and the goal card's goal set from feedback; DA:Pr4.1.5a, a look-for: ground and air paths with eye focus and projection; DA:Pr4.1.5b, a look-for: the group dances to its own body percussion and a found-sound rhythm and keeps on when the teacher changes the timing; DA:Pr5.1.5b, a written item: from a new invented dancer's card, two safe habits and how they and food help prevent injury; DA:Pr4.1.5c, a show item and a written item: one move shown tight and then flowing at the teacher's spot, saying where it starts, and one line analyzing the energy of the teacher's unseen phrase. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: partner and group sections in measures of three and four (grade 6). Tools: the run card, goal card, body-percussion card and invented dancer card, Curio Class's own; a beat keeper or a hand drum. Free path: plastic tubs, paper and the body for found sound. Once-a-week path: 9 sessions | First in grade 5 because it reopens the dance space, and the ensemble habits and goal card carry every later rehearsal of the year; 17 days because a run of phrases rehearsed to goals needs a second rehearsal cycle after the critique. The rehearsal-goals model starts here | Candidate: the found-sound kit checked by the safety agent item by item | Food: no task asks about a student's own diet, weight or body; nutrition is studied through the invented dancer only (APPROACH "Sensitive ground"). Sasa: the sensitivity agent reads a Samoan cultural body's or a museum's page first; no costume; slaps gentle, on the student's own thighs and the floor. Found sound: plastic tubs, paper and soft sticks only; no metal lids, bins or glass; a 