82:   check is a short Curio Class original danced live by the teacher from a picture step card, or a short written
83:   description read aloud, never an embed (APPROACH "Scoring creative work"). Curio Class writes every step card,
84:   work card, challenge card, research card, map sheet, record sheet, family note and every unseen dance.
85: - **Techniques that get harder (bar criterion 2).** Body and space: a sequence copied with the body aligned, partner
86:   level and path changes, an improvisation that fills a set count (3); balance in recalled patterns, moving together
87:   on a cue, a drum part played for others, soft landings (4); a run of phrases rehearsed as an ensemble, body
88:   percussion and found sound, ground and air paths, tight against flowing (5). Making: a challenge solved, AB and ABA
89:   forms with repetition and reversal (3); a challenge invented for a partner, a study around one main idea with a
90:   tool altered (4); material from several sources, several challenges in a group, a study whose tools change together
91:   (5). Changing and recording: a change after partner feedback and a floor map of paths (3); a rework from comments
92:   and reflection and a relationship sketch (4); peer suggestions tried and a change log (5). Performing: stage areas
93:   named and one design choice (3); a gym or lawn planned as a stage and production elements tried (4); one dance
94:   adapted to two venues (5).
