261: | This course hands on | Unit here | Row that picks it up (Dance 6 to 8 unit) | What grade 6 does with it |
262: |---|---|---|---|
263: | da-g5-technique | 9 | da-g6-technique (unit 1) | Clean direction changes, jumps, landings and transitions; a warm-up understood through the body's signals; an ensemble dance improved by testing fixes |
264: | da-g5-elements | 9 | da-g6-elements (unit 1) | Partner and group sections, sudden and sustained timing in three- and four-beat music, muscle tension for dynamics |
265: | da-g5-ideas | 10 | da-g6-ideas (unit 2) | Ideas joined by likeness or contrast, and styles tried on purpose |
266: | da-g5-connect | 10 | da-g6-connect (unit 4) | A viewpoint on a researched social issue danced, tastes compared in a log, a dance's meaning to its community |
267: | da-g5-form | 11 | da-g6-form (unit 2) | A study toward a goal the student sets, with the student's own criteria |
268: | da-g5-respond | 11 | da-g6-respond (unit 3) | A written critique with criteria the student drafts |
269: | da-g5-revise | 12 | da-g6-revise (unit 3) | Revision against group-built criteria, and the student's own way of writing down moves |
270: | da-g5-stage | 12 | da-g6-stage (unit 4) | Performance manners, the choreographer's notes, production elements compared in production terms |

