## For the lead

1. **After-core check weeks.** This frame's checks (mid-year week 17, school days 83 and 85, and year-end week 32,
   in each of grades 6, 7 and 8) stay off every core check week and day, and follow from the unit days by load.
   Left for the lead's one calendar pass over all after-core frames: week 17 also holds health's and physical
   education's mid-year checks in all three grades (their day 84, between this frame's days 83 and 85).
2. **Physical education frame's pending line.** docs/courses/physical-education-grades-6-to-8/frame.md, Cross-subject,
   "After-core courses": its pending note on dance's units and weeks can now be replaced with "Dance 6 to 8 teaches its rows first in each year: units 1 and 2 (grade
   6 weeks 1 to 16), units 5 and 6 (grade 7 weeks 1 to 16), unit 9 (grade 8 weeks 1 to 9); its picks differ from
   physical education's." The same table's last row should name dance's technique rows too (da-g6-technique,
   da-g7-technique, da-g8-technique), which carry the progression's physical education leans.
3. **Row changes.** Two rows' descriptions are narrower than their ids, one row's evidence wording needs a recording
   the paper path lacks, and six rows' "Assessed by" notes miss an id; the frame teaches and checks the full ids. The
   row changes are in the writer's final message (da-g6-elements, da-g6-technique, da-g8-respond, and the "Assessed
   by" notes of da-g6-technique, da-g7-technique, da-g8-technique, da-g6-connect, da-g7-connect, da-g8-connect).
4. **Works checked at source.** The works are picked from what is known of them, not opened for this frame (no web
   reads). The unit plan opens each holding page for its rights line and title, as the pilot's fix pass did: the
   Tang dancer figurine and the court ballet's costume designs (open-access images), the Dance Notation Bureau's
   pages, the Smithsonian's National Museum of the American Indian pages on the fancy shawl dance, UNESCO's capoeira
   and tango pages, and each company's or maker's page (Sankai Juku, Kaha:wi Dance Theatre, Shen Wei Dance Arts, Rosy Simas Danse,
   Rennie Harris Puremovement, Mark Morris Dance Group, the Moiseyev company, Rosas, Ballet Hispánico, Camille A.
   Brown and Dancers, Studios Kabako). Each pick was checked against the K to 2 and 3 to 5 dance
   frames' works, and none repeats.
5. **Unseen dances.** As in the K to 2 dance frame: every unseen dance is a Curio Class original danced live by the
   teacher from a step card, or a written description. A filmed set of the band's 24 or so unseen phrases would
   help a teacher with no dance training, but needs a dancer and filming (a people and money question for Cory).
6. **Supplies ceiling (money, for Cory).** Provisional costs: $30 (year 6), $25 (year 7), $30 (year 8) a class of 30,
   all optional beside a free path. Pick: the same ceiling as the K to 2 dance pick, $50 a class a year, with every
   unit's free path kept.


