1. **Pattern copied from the K to 2 pilot.** One file with a Year column, each year whole; every year ends on short
   units after its year-end check (week 26), because K to 5 weeks 28 to 32 are mostly core check weeks; each unit's
   Ends names one skill task, one knowledge task and one S3 behavior; across a year's two checks every standard is
   sampled from units before the check; the short path is computed from this band's own dose. Dose kept at the
   APPROACH default (80 x 35).
2. **Check weeks, one pattern for all three years.** Mid-year days 43 to 45 (week 18) and year-end days 63 to 65
   (week 26) are off every core check week of grades 3, 4 and 5, respond days included, so the K to 2 frame's
   respond-day question (its For the lead 5) does not arise here.
